    "result_text": "No stale references. The change is complete. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived owner values onto a **fiscal-year basis** (fiscal year starts 1 July, identified by the calendar year it begins in). All derivations key off the already business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` that `ClinicServiceImpl` stores on the owner.\n\n**New single-responsibility utility \u2014 `util/FiscalYear.java`:**\n- `startingYear(date)` \u2014 the calendar year the containing fiscal year began (date's year if month \u2265 July, else previous year).\n- `label(date)` \u2014 formats as `FY<YY>` (null-safe).\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years between two dates (July-1 boundaries crossed), never negative.\n\n**Reused it across the existing logic instead of duplicating date math:**\n- `MembershipNumberFormatter` \u2014 the `M<YY>` segment now uses `FiscalYear.startingYear(...)` rather than the raw calendar year.\n- `OwnerTenure` \u2014 `inDays(...)` replaced by `inFiscalYears(...)`, delegating to `FiscalYear.elapsed(...)`.\n- `MembershipPointsFormatter` \u2014 the tenure points now trigger once tenure exceeds one fiscal year (threshold constant retyped from days to fiscal years).\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 added the new `fiscalYear` mapping via `FiscalYear.label(...)`.\n\n**Spec/DTO:**\n- Added the `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`) property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (the `OwnerDto` is generated from it), and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\n`OwnerAuditLogger` needed no change \u2014 it already reuses the formatters, so its logged membership number/points now reflect the fiscal year automatically (confirmed in the run: `registrationDate=2026-09-21 \u2026 membershipNumber=\u2026-M26`).\n\nTest suite: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 including the new `coreReturnsFiscalYear` acceptance check.",
